course: dictionary
lesson: 6806
title: Groups, plans and order
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: The word «organization» has three meanings. It can be a group of people who work together for a purpose, such as a charity or a club. It can be the planning and arranging of things so they work well. It can also be the way something is arranged or put together.
explain: Use the context to choose the meaning. «The World Health Organization helped to wipe out smallpox.» Health and wiping out smallpox are clues that this is a group of people working together, so organization means a group here. Swap in your meaning: "The World Health Organization helped, as a group that works together for a purpose" still makes sense.
explain: Other clues point to planning. A child with her bag packed and homework planned for the week shows good organization. Ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence, then check it by putting your meaning in place of the word.
fact: An organization is a group of people who work together for a purpose, such as a charity, a club, a company or a school.
fact: Organization can mean planning and arranging things so they work well, such as having your bag packed and your homework planned.
fact: Organization can also mean the way something is arranged or put together, such as the order of ideas in a text.
fact: Phrases to know: «a charity organization», «good organization», «lack of organization», «the World Health Organization».
fact: When you mean the skill of planning, you say «good organization», without «a» in front.
exercise: «The World Health Organization helped to wipe out smallpox.» What is an organization here? | *A group of people who work together for a purpose | The order of paragraphs in a story | A tidy bag with the books in order | A kind of storm
exercise: Mia always has her bag packed and her homework planned for the week. Which meaning of organization fits here? | *Planning and arranging things so they work well | The last paragraph of a text | A group of people who work together for a purpose | A place where storms are named
exercise: Which of these is an organization in the first meaning? | The sky on a sunny day | *The Red Cross, a charity | A bell that rings at the start of lessons | A pile of books on a desk
test: «The World Food Programme» works on hunger around the world. Why is it called an organization? | Because it lists the storms of the year | *Because it is a group of people who work together for a purpose | Because it is always tidy | Because it has big letters in its name
test: A writer puts her paragraphs in the right order, so her story is clear. This shows good organization. Which meaning is this? | A list of storm names made in advance | *The way something is arranged or put together | A group of people who work together | A charity that helps children
exam: Which sentence uses organization to mean a group of people? | *The Met Office is an organization that names UK storms | Her room shows good organization | Organization is the order of paragraphs in a text | Lack of organization made her late
